1. lugal iri ab₂-gin₇ lu-a [unudₓ(UNU₃) X X za-e]-me#-en
#tr.en: O king, you are the …… shepherd of the city which thrives like cattle!
#lem: lugal[king]; iri[city]; ab[cow]; lu[abundant]; unud[cowherd]; X; X; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru (N3), 0.2.06, line 17

2. {d}nin-a-zu iri ab₂-gin₇ [lu-a unudₓ(UNU₃) X X za]-e-me-en
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninazu}, you are the …… shepherd of the city which thrives like cattle!
#lem: Ninazu[1]DN; iri[city]; ab[cow]; lu[abundant]; unud[cowherd]; X; X; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. en {d}nin-a-zu-ŋu₁₀ <iri> ab₂-[gin₇ lu-a] unud(UNU₃)# [X X za]-e-me-en
#tr.en: My lord @wDN{Ninazu}, you are the …… shepherd of the city which thrives like cattle!
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; iri[city]; ab[cow]; lu[abundant]; unud[cowherd]; X; X; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. {gi}kid za-gin₃-na-gin₇ X [...] X ad-KID X-bi za-e-me-en
#tr.en: You are the reed-worker of the ……, …… like a shining mat!
#lem: kid[reed mat or woven object]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; X; X; X; ad.KID[basket weaver]; X; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. udu-gin₇ amaš-e ri#-[a dur₂]-ru-na-dur₂-<ru-na> na-gada-bi za-e-me-en
#tr.en: You are the herdsman of them that dwell like sheep in a sheepfold,
#lem: udu[sheep]; amaš[sheepfold]; ri[impose]; durun[sit]; nagada[herdsman]; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. hur-saŋ sukud-ra₂ ul gur₃-ru en {d}nin-a-zu-me-en
#tr.en: you who exude the allure of the high hills, Lord @wDN{Ninazu}!
#lem: hursaŋ[mountain]; sukud[height]; ul[swell]; gur[lift]; en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. en# {d}nin-a-zu ki-in-du ha-ba-dim₂-ma {d}nanna he₂-e-da-hul₂
#tr.en: Lord @wDN{Ninazu}, may @wDN{Nanna} rejoice over you that the earth was created. Powerful and of great intelligence, you were engendered by @wDN{Nanna}.
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; kindu[earth]; dim[create]; Nanna[1]DN; hul[rejoice]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. uru₁₇ umuš gal-la {d}nanna tud#-[da]-me-en
#tr.en: May @wDN{Ašimbabbar} make the shining branches of your sceptre radiant in your grasp. He has strengthened the foundations of the throne which @wDN{An} gave you.
#lem: urun[exalted]; umuš[consideration]; gal[big]; Nanna[1]DN; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. pa mul-zu {d}dil-im₂-babbar-re a₂ he₂-em-mi-ni-in-rin₂-rin₂#-ne₂#
#tr.en: May he make the way straight for you as far as the ends of heaven and earth,
#lem: pa[branch]; mul[shine]; Dilimbabbar[1]DN; a[arm]; girim[clear]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. {ŋiš}gu-za an-ne₂ ma-ra-an-šum₂-ma-zu suhuš-bi nam#-[mi-in-gen₆]
#tr.en: may he make it as straight for you as the sunlight. My lord @wDN{Ninazu},
#lem: guza[chair]; An[1]DN; šum[give]; suhuš[foundation]; gin[confirm]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. zag an ki-še₃ ŋiri₃ si he₂-da-ab-sa₂ ud-gin₇ si he₂-da-ab-sa₂#
#tr.en: may he make it as straight for you as the sunlight,
#lem: zag[side]; an[sky]; ki[place]; ŋiri[foot]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; ud[sun]; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. en {d}nin#-[a]-zu#-ŋu₁₀ ud-gin₇ si ha-ra-ab-sa₂ ud-gin₇ si ha#-[ra-ab-sa₂]
#tr.en: may he make it as straight for you as the sunlight.
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; ud[sun]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; ud[sun]; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. {d}suen#-[e] šibir# nam-en-na#-zu šu im-mi-du₇
#tr.en: @wDN{Suen} has perfected your lordly staff,
#lem: Suen[1]DN; šibir[shepherd's staff]; namen[the office of en-priest]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. {ŋiš}ŋidru mah kur-kur-ra pa e₃ uŋ₃-e im-mi-lah₆
#tr.en: the lofty sceptre which shines over all the foreign countries, and guides the people.
#lem: ŋidru[scepter]; mah[great]; kur[mountain(s)]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; uŋ[people]; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. {d}lamma-zu e₂-kiš-nu-ŋal₂-la a₂ gal ha-ra-an-X-a
#tr.en: Your protective goddess has …… great power for you in @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}.
#lem: lammar[(female) tutelary deity]; Ekišnuŋal[1]TN; a[arm]; gal[big]; X
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. {d}nin-a-zu urim₂{ki}-ma tud-da {d}nanna he₂-e-[da-hul₂]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninazu}, born in @wSN{Urim}, may @wDN{Nanna} rejoice over you.
#lem: Ninazu[1]DN; Urim[1]SN; utud[give birth (to)]; Nanna[1]DN; hul[rejoice]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. en {d}nin-a-zu urim₂{ki}-ma tud-da {d}nanna he₂-e-da-hul₂
#tr.en: Lord @wDN{Ninazu}, born in @wSN{Urim}, may @wDN{Nanna} rejoice over you.
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; Urim[1]SN; utud[give birth (to)]; Nanna[1]DN; hul[rejoice]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. a-a ugu-zu kur gal {d}en-lil₂-le mu-zu pa bi₂-in-e₃
#tr.en: The father who engendered you, the Great Mountain @wDN{Enlil}, has made your name glorious.
#lem: aya[father]; ugu[bear]; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]; Enlil[1]DN; mu[name]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. ama ugu-zu nin mah ki-ur₃-ra nam-zu mu-[ra-ni-tar]
#tr.en: Your own mother, the august lady, has decided your destiny in the @wTN{Ki-ur}.
#lem: ama[mother]; ugu[bear]; nin[lady]; mah[great]; Kiʾur[1]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. e₂-zu iri-zu kur [ki] sikil-ta ki-[tuš-bi] hu-mu-un-ŋa₂-[ŋa₂]
#tr.en: May you take your seat in your house, in your city -- the mountain, the pure place!
#lem: e[house]; iri[city]; kur[mountain(s)]; ki[place]; sikil[pure]; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. enegir{ki} iri-zu# kur ki sikil-ta [ki-tuš-bi] hu-mu-un-ŋa₂#-[ŋa₂]
#tr.en: May you take your seat in @wSN{Enegir}, in your city -- the mountain, the pure place!
#lem: Enegir[1]SN; iri[city]; kur[mountain(s)]; ki[place]; sikil[pure]; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. en {d}nin-a-zu-ŋu₁₀ ki-tuš-bi hu-mu-[un]-ŋa₂-[ŋa₂] ki-tuš-bi hu-mu-un-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: My lord @wDN{Ninazu}, may you take your seat there, may you take your seat there!
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. aga kug-sig₁₇ saŋ-za ma-ra-ni-in-gen₆ šu zid ma-ra-ni-in-du₇
#tr.en: He has fixed the golden headdress on your head, making you truly perfect with it.
#lem: aga[tiara]; kugsig[gold]; saŋ[head]; gin[confirm]; šu[hand]; zid[right]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. dumu nir-ŋal₂ a-a ugu-na-ke₄ šag₄ ki aŋ₂-ŋa₂ bi₂-X
#tr.en: He has …… the lordly son of his own father, the beloved of his heart.
#lem: dumu[child]; nirŋal[authoritative]; aya[father]; ugu[bear]; šag[heart]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; X
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. [...]-ni# igi saŋ-ŋa₂ mu-ši-in-bar
#tr.en: He has looked with best favour on ……. @wDN{An} has determined a good destiny for you.
#lem: X; igi[eye]; saŋ[choose]; bar[place outside]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. [an]-ne₂# nam dug₃ mu-ri-in-tar
#tr.en: Son of @wDN{Enlil} king of the lands, may your splendour shine forth!
#lem: An[1]DN; nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. [dumu] {[d]}en-[lil₂] lugal kur-kur-ra-ka me-lem₄-zu he₂-e₃
#tr.en: My lord @wDN{Ninazu}, may your splendour shine forth, may your splendour shine forth!
#lem: dumu[child]; Enlil[1]DN; lugal[king]; kur[mountain(s)]; melim[frightening splendor]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. [en] {[d]}[nin]-a-zu-ŋu₁₀ me-lem₄-zu he₂-e₃ me-lem₄-zu he₂-e₃
#tr.en: May your wife, the maiden, the good woman, Lady @wDN{Ningirida},
#lem: en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN; melim[frightening splendor]; e[leave]; melim[frightening splendor]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. nitalam#-zu ki-sikil munus sag₉-ga nin {d}nin-girid₂-da
#tr.en: say to you: @q[Ningirida,Ninazu]{“Your house, your city!”}
#lem: ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; kisikil[young woman]; munus[woman]; sag[good]; nin[lady]; Ningirida[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. e₂-zu iri-zu hu-mu-ra-ab-be₂ šita-še₃ ša-ra-da-gub
#tr.en: as she steps before you in prayer,
#lem: e[house]; iri[city]; e[speak]; šita[prayer]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. [diŋir] kalam#-ma en {d}nin-a-zu-ŋu₁₀
#tr.en: god of the Land, my lord @wDN{Ninazu}!
#lem: diŋir[deity]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; en[lord]; Ninazu[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=31

